<header class="ats-guide-intro"><span class="reference-eyebrow">UNDERSTANDING OUR SERVICE</span><h1>Terms and Conditions</h1><p class="policy-status">Effective date: 22 October 2026</p><p>These terms apply to <strong>atscvdetector.com</strong>, provided by <strong>atscvdetector</strong> (“we”, “us” or “our”). “You” means the person using atscvdetector. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>.</p></header>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>1. Agreement and related policies</h2><p>Read these terms before creating an account or requesting a service. By taking either action, you agree to these terms. If you disagree, do not create an account or request a service. Our <a href="{{ route('privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a> explains personal information processing, and our <a href="{{ route('refund') }}">Refund Policy</a> explains payment remedies. Nothing here removes rights that applicable law does not allow us to exclude.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>2. Our services</h2><p>atscvdetector provides digital CV and resume tools: CV building, document import and export, comparison with job descriptions, formatting assistance and optional AI-assisted rewriting. Access depends on feature availability, account requirements and the limits shown in the service. Upcoming features are not a promise of immediate availability.</p><p>We help you prepare and assess career documents. We are not an employer, recruitment agency, placement service, immigration adviser or an employer's Applicant Tracking System. These tools do not submit applications or contact employers for you.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>3. ATS estimates and employment outcomes</h2><p>A match score estimates how your CV aligns with detected job requirements, including qualifications, skills and competencies, using the information supplied. It is not a count of every word in the advert. It is not an employer's ATS score, a certification, an assessment of your fitness for a role or a hiring decision. Employers use different systems, screening questions and selection criteria that may be unknown to us.</p><p>“ATS-friendly” describes an effort to improve readable structure and relevant wording. We do not guarantee compatibility with every ATS, a particular score, an interview, an offer, a salary, a visa or employment. A higher score does not necessarily mean a stronger application.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>4. Eligibility and account security</h2><p>You must be at least 18 and able to enter a binding agreement to create an account. Supply accurate account information, keep credentials secure and report suspected unauthorised access promptly. Do not impersonate another person or share access to evade service limits. If you choose Google sign-in, Google's own account terms also apply.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>5. Your content and responsibilities</h2><p>Submit only material you own or are authorised to use. Have a lawful basis for including another person's information, such as referee details. Remove unnecessary identity numbers, financial details, medical information and other sensitive data.</p><p>Keep your CV truthful. Review names, contact details, dates, qualifications, skills and achievements before downloading or applying. You decide which suggestions to accept and remain responsible for the application you submit. Keep your own copies of important documents.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>6. AI and document conversion</h2><p>Optional AI tools use an external service provider to process submitted content. Generated wording can contain errors, omissions, unsupported claims or unsuitable language. Treat it as a draft, not verified fact or professional advice. Do not accept invented experience, qualifications or results.</p><p>Imports and exports may change formatting, omit text or misidentify fields. Scans and complex layouts may not be readable. Inspect the editor and the final file, including page breaks and content order. Any processing-time estimate depends on the document, network and external services and is not a guaranteed delivery time.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>7. Acceptable use</h2><p>Do not use the service for fraud, unlawful discrimination, harassment, infringement, malware or unauthorised disclosure of personal data. Do not bypass account controls, access other people's records, overload the service or automate requests to evade limits. Report security concerns through support without accessing or copying another user's information.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>8. Plans, prices and payments</h2><p>Available plans and payment methods are shown at checkout. Creating an account or viewing a plan does not authorise a charge. Free accounts receive 15 welcome credits once. Job-to-CV ATS Detector costs 5 credits and a CV revamp costs 10 credits; manual editing and downloads use no credits. Subscription credits are allocated for the relevant monthly period and unused subscription credits expire at the end of the paid term. Early renewal makes the additional credits available immediately and preserves the remaining subscription balance until the extended paid term ends. Separately purchased top-up credits, where offered, carry over subject to account and payment status. Annual plans provide 2,400 credits available when the paid year begins, valid until that paid year ends.</p><p>Before payment, the order screen shows the service, total price, currency, applicable taxes and fees, delivery details and any renewal or cancellation terms. Paynow payments are one-time purchases with manual renewal and no automatic deductions. Our <a href="{{ route('refund') }}">Refund Policy</a> applies to verified purchases. The current Pricing page and checkout describe the plan, included templates, allowances and term. Free includes seven selected templates. Viewing a plan or using welcome credits does not authorise payment.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>9. Payment confirmation, currencies and credit accounting</h2><p>Paid access and credits are granted after successful provider verification. A pending bank authorisation, receipt email or redirect alone may not prove that the app has verified the transaction. If a successful payment is missing from your account, contact support with the transaction reference rather than paying repeatedly for the same order.</p><p>The amount and currency shown before authorising payment govern the transaction. Any currency conversion shown is not a guarantee of your bank's exchange rate or foreign-transaction fees. Payment details are entered with the selected provider; never send payment PINs, banking passwords or card security codes to support.</p><p>Credits are service units, not money or a direct conversion of AI tokens. They are not transferable and cannot be withdrawn as cash. Displayed operation costs apply before use, and prospective changes will be disclosed appropriately. Payment remedies remain available under the Refund Policy.</p><p>The app records credit reservations, completed use and reversals for failed operations. Report a missing reversal for investigation. A refunded or reversed purchase can cause corresponding access or credit adjustments so that the same payment cannot provide duplicate benefits.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>10. Renewal and cancellation</h2><p>Automatic renewal applies only where disclosed and authorised in the selected payment flow. Some payment methods are one-time purchases. Review your payment confirmation rather than assuming all methods renew. Available methods and current payment status are shown at checkout.</p><p>Stop future renewals through the available Subscription controls, or email support if you need assistance. Check that cancellation is confirmed before the next scheduled charge. Cancellation normally leaves access available until the paid term ends unless a refund or payment reversal changes your entitlement. Cancelling renewal is different from requesting a refund for a previous charge.</p><p>Stop active automatic renewals before account deletion; contact support if you cannot access cancellation controls. Deleting a CV, clearing browser data or not using the app does not cancel a provider's recurring instruction. If you want cancellation and a refund, clearly request both.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>11. Template permissions and fair use</h2><p>You may use permitted templates to create and download your career documents. This permission does not allow resale of the template library, redistribution of underlying assets or publication of the app as your own product. Do not bypass paid-template restrictions, scrape the library, exploit payment errors or create multiple accounts to repeatedly claim welcome benefits.</p><p>We cannot guarantee that browser protections prevent every screenshot or copy. That technical limitation does not grant permission to redistribute protected designs or another person's content. A legitimate customer complaint is not, by itself, a breach of fair-use rules.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>12. Refunds, service changes and disputes</h2><p>Monthly and Pro monthly plans are non-refundable, including unused purchases and renewals, except for billing corrections or refunds required by applicable law. Only an eligible first Annual plan purchase receives the seven-day unused-purchase refund window described in the Refund Policy. Cancelling renewal does not refund the current paid period. The Refund Policy also explains completed services, billing mistakes and technical faults. A correctly completed AI service is not routinely refunded simply because you change your mind, but faults, misleading descriptions and statutory remedies are assessed on their merits. Using AI or downloading output does not automatically waive mandatory rights.</p><p>If we discontinue a prepaid service during its term and cannot provide an agreed suitable alternative, we will assess the undelivered portion under the Refund Policy. A refund or provider reversal for the same payment will not be paid twice. Where proportionate and lawful, benefits directly related to a disputed payment may be restricted during investigation. We will not treat a good-faith dispute as proof of fraud.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>13. Ownership and permission to process</h2><p>You retain your rights in content you submit. You give us limited permission to store, reproduce, convert and process it, including through necessary providers, to deliver your requested features, secure the service and comply with law. This permission does not authorise selling your CV or publishing it as a testimonial. Retention and disclosure are explained in the Privacy Policy.</p><p>You may use your generated CV for lawful purposes, subject to existing third-party rights. AI output may not be unique and exclusive intellectual property rights in it are not guaranteed. Our original software, branding, designs and written site content belong to the respective rights holders or licensors. Third-party materials retain their respective rights.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>14. Availability, suspension and closure</h2><p>Maintenance, faults and external outages can interrupt service. We may change features or reasonable usage limits, without removing remedies for services already purchased. We may restrict access when reasonably necessary to address abuse, security risks or a breach of these terms. Where appropriate, we will explain the restriction and allow you to contact support; urgent legal or security circumstances may require immediate action.</p><p>You may stop using the service and request account deletion. Account restrictions do not automatically remove refund or consumer rights. Back up your documents before closing your account.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>15. Service standards and liability</h2><p>We will exercise reasonable care and skill, subject to any stronger standard required by law. Beyond express commitments and mandatory rights, we do not promise uninterrupted operation, error-free outputs or fitness for every personal purpose.</p><p>To the extent permitted by law, we are not responsible for indirect or consequential losses, lost employment opportunities or independent employer decisions. This does not exclude a remedy merely because AI was involved, or exclude liability for fraud, deliberate misconduct, gross negligence or anything that cannot lawfully be limited. Mandatory consumer protections prevail over conflicting wording here.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>16. Questions, complaints and disputes</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a> with your account email, a description of the issue and any order reference. Never send passwords or full payment credentials. We aim to acknowledge complaints within five business days and provide an outcome or progress update within fourteen business days. These targets do not restrict your rights.</p><p>Applicable law determines your rights and the competent forum. These terms do not remove mandatory consumer protections. You may bring a dispute before a court with lawful jurisdiction or use a competent regulator or payment-provider dispute process. We do not require compulsory private arbitration or a waiver of those rights.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>17. Updates and interpretation</h2><p>We will date revised terms and give reasonable notice of material changes through the site or account communications where appropriate. Changes apply prospectively and do not retrospectively remove purchase rights. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining terms continue insofar as law permits. Delayed enforcement is not a waiver.</p><p>For an explanation of any clause before requesting a service, contact support at <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>.</p></section>
